STATUS: PHYSICS DEFECT — MUST BE CORRECTED.

The jellyfish-like floating platform is called Drifter.

The user reported that it glitches and changes position
unnaturally.

Inspect:

src/game/entities/creatures/Drifter.ts

src/game/scenes/GameplayScene.ts

CURRENT CONFIRMED CODE CONCERN:

Drifter.update() currently manually changes position
using sprite.setPosition() and also applies velocity
through body.setVelocity() based on the same displacement.

This creates two movement authorities.

The physics engine may subsequently integrate the
velocity and move the object again.

The player-carry collider callback also only applies
drifter.deltaX.

It ignores vertical displacement.

This is an important reason the moving platform and
passenger may become visually desynchronized.

REQUIRED ARCHITECTURE:

Choose ONE authoritative movement system.

Option A:
Physics-driven moving platform using Arcade Physics.

Option B:
Properly synchronized kinematic platform with controlled
body position updates and passenger carrying.

Never manually apply the same displacement and then
allow physics to integrate that displacement again.

